; What our kernel32.dll exports (docs/abi/windows.md W2): every name must be
; defined in kernel32.c. A program importing anything else is bound to one of
; ntdll's named stubs and says which when it calls it.
LIBRARY kernel32.dll
EXPORTS
CloseHandle
CreateDirectoryA
CreateDirectoryW
CreateEventA
CreateEventW
CreateFileA
CreateFileMappingA
CreateFileMappingW
CreateFileW
CreateMutexA
CreateMutexW
CreateSemaphoreA
CreateSemaphoreW
CreateThread
DeleteFileA
DeleteFileW
DuplicateHandle
ExitProcess
FindClose
FindFirstFileA
FindFirstFileW
FindNextFileA
FindNextFileW
FlushFileBuffers
FreeLibrary
GetCurrentProcess
GetCurrentProcessId
GetCurrentThread
GetCurrentThreadId
GetEnvironmentVariableA
GetEnvironmentVariableW
GetErrorMode
GetFileAttributesA
GetFileAttributesExA
GetFileAttributesExW
GetFileAttributesW
GetFileSize
GetFileSizeEx
GetLastError
GetModuleHandleA
GetModuleHandleW
GetNativeSystemInfo
GetProcAddress
GetProcessHeap
GetStdHandle
GetSystemInfo
GetTickCount
GetTickCount64
HeapAlloc
HeapFree
HeapReAlloc
HeapSize
HeapValidate
IsBadStringPtrA
IsBadStringPtrW
LoadLibraryA
LoadLibraryW
MapViewOfFile
MapViewOfFileEx
MoveFileA
MoveFileW
OpenEventA
OpenEventW
OpenFileMappingA
OpenFileMappingW
OpenMutexA
OpenMutexW
PulseEvent
ReadFile
ReleaseMutex
ReleaseSemaphore
RemoveDirectoryA
RemoveDirectoryW
ResetEvent
SetEndOfFile
SetErrorMode
SetEvent
SetFilePointer
SetFilePointerEx
SetLastError
SetUnhandledExceptionFilter
Sleep
SleepEx
TlsAlloc
TlsFree
TlsGetValue
TlsSetValue
UnmapViewOfFile
VirtualAlloc
VirtualAllocEx
VirtualFree
VirtualFreeEx
VirtualProtect
VirtualProtectEx
VirtualQuery
VirtualQueryEx
WaitForMultipleObjects
WaitForMultipleObjectsEx
WaitForSingleObject
WaitForSingleObjectEx
WriteFile
